WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.020
Dr. Jack Bright is one of the Foundation’s
most enigmatic and chaotic figures.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.380
Infamous for being the subject of a humorous
joke file passed between personnel titled

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:16.179
“The Things Dr. Bright Is Not Allowed To
Do At The Foundation”, which describes…

00:00:16.179 --> 00:00:18.050
well, exactly that.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:22.400
By reading the list, you’d get the idea
that this Dr. Bright fellow is a pretty fun

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:27.769
and goofy guy, certainly popular enough to
get an entire list that has himself as the

00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:32.500
sole punchline, but while that much is true,
it’s not the whole story.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.640
Sure, he’s a strange man with an even stranger
sense of humor, but a lot of that apparent

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.829
weirdness comes from Jack Bright’s experiences
throughout his life.

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:44.320
Or lives, we should say.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.399
We’ll explain.

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:49.140
Needless to say, he has quite the story to
tell.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.920
For starters, Dr. Jack Bright is immortal.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.489
Not in the sense that he cannot die, but that
his soul itself is permanently affixed to

00:00:56.489 --> 00:01:00.719
an amulet, which has been given the designation
SCP-963-1.

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:06.560
Originally, the amulet was in the possession
of the Foundation as a minor anomalous object

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.440
that was incapable of being damaged.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:15.890
While Dr. Bright was transporting the amulet,
the deadly warrior, SCP-076-2, nicknamed Able,

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:20.280
broke free from its resting coffin and went
on a murderous rampage throughout the facility.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:26.049
Dr. Bright, who was holding SCP-963-1, was
one of the first killed in action.

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:31.070
Days later, after the chaos had subsided,
a Foundation rescue team recovered Bright’s

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:35.100
body from the wreckage, with SCP-963-1 along
with it.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:40.140
When the D-Class operative who stumbled upon
the amulet put it on, he gained the memories,

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:43.270
personality, and consciousness of Jack Bright.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:47.540
The mind of the D-Class was wiped entirely,
and only Bright remained.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:52.369
When the amulet was removed, the D-Class went
into a vegetative state, ceasing all brain

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:53.399
activity.

00:01:53.399 --> 00:01:57.360
Thanks to SCP-963-1, Dr. Bright is immortal.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.750
His consciousness is stored in the amulet
itself, and transfers to whoever puts it on.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:07.110
After a 30 day period of wearing the amulet,
the new body’s brain will become a duplicate

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:11.740
of the late Dr. Bright’s, even when the
amulet is removed from their person.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:15.920
This could effectively allow a whole number
of Dr. Brights to run wildly around the Foundation

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.100
if left unchecked.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.640
Thankfully, the Foundation has many safety
measures in place to prevent exactly that

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:26.330
from happening, such as limiting the current
Bright host body to one person and keeping

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:29.700
an eye on which body Bright is presently occupying.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.980
Unfortunately, this hasn’t always worked.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:40.290
As you’ll see in today’s SCP briefing:
SCP-4498: The Plurality of Jack Bright.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.730
Being immortal has a few downsides.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:46.720
For one, Bright feels tied to the amulet,
unable to be released.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:50.640
He’s occupied countless bodies, and longs
for a way out.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.220
Deep down, he’s aware that he may never
truly die.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.420
Doomed to a fate of eternal body switching
until the universe burns out.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.610
Maybe that’s where Bright’s goofiness
comes from.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:05.250
He plays the act of a clown to hide the pain
and tragedy of his life.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:09.860
Regardless of how Bright may act, no one can
deny that his story isn’t tragic.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:13.210
But this particular event was a little less
than tragic.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.700
In fact, it was a Bright overload.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:20.670
The exact kind of scenario the Foundation
wanted to prevent through their containment

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:27.100
procedures of SCP-963-, and the tracking of
which body Bright was currently occupying.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.870
In fact, that’s what SCP-4498 is.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:37.170
It’s the designation given to a group of
over 325 men, women, animals, and anomalous

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:43.290
entities who were previously assigned to Foundation
facility Site-53 who now assume the consciousness

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.110
of Dr. Jack Bright.

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:47.450
But how did this happen?

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.750
More importantly, how does the Foundation
keep such a wild array of characters contained?

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:57.750
Well, since SCP-4498 makes up the entire personnel
of a former Site, the Foundation was able

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:03.260
to establish a Quarantined Exclusion Zone
where Site-53 used to be.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:07.800
Interaction with the Bright instances was
limited to only necessary communications,

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:13.830
and separation of an SCP-4498 instance from
the Quarantined Exclusion Zone was not permitted.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:18.030
In case any of the instances acted out of
line, as Dr. Bright tends to do this from

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:24.290
time to time, an Applied Task Force, named
Bright-99 "Oh No You Don't", was created to

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:30.480
subdue any rowdy Brights and keep them where
they belong through the use of nonlethal means.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.480
Until the Foundation is able to find a way
to neutralize the effects of SCP-4498, the

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:41.900
former personnel of Site-53 are stuck in containment,
harboring the consciousness of Jack Bright.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.820
But again, how did this even happen?

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:51.160
On May 9th, 2018, an unexpected interaction
between a now-neutralized anomaly and SCP-963-1

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:56.900
at Site-53 resulted in the creation of this
quirky anomaly.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:01.070
Bright had been assigned to the facility because
of his expertise regarding a certain anomaly

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:06.040
they were studying, a small porcelain cat
statue that appeared to negate or depress

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:10.210
the effects of nearby anomalies when its tail
was turned clockwise.

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:14.880
But on that day, when Dr. Bright arrived at
work, he mishandled the object.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.910
Instead of turning the tail clockwise, he
turned it counterclockwise by accident.

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:24.230
This resulted in the tail breaking off of
the statue and triggering a new, never before

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:32.180
seen anomalous effect that amplified and engulfed
the entire Site once it interacted with SCP-963-1,

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.760
the amulet hanging from Bright’s neck.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:39.020
Upon breaking the tail, the lights in Site-53
flickered and all personnel collapsed to the

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.770
floor and the security cameras lost power.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:45.720
When the security cameras rebooted, all personnel
were standing straight up.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:50.010
There was immediate confusion, especially
among the research team who was observing

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:51.790
Bright’s inspection of the anomaly.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.360
They weren’t sure what happened.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:56.340
One researcher suggested that they had all
swapped bodies.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:59.420
Another was confused as to why he was in his
current body.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:03.410
On the count of three, the researchers decided
to shout out their names, just to see who

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.330
ended up in whose body.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:09.810
On three, they all yelled the same name: Jack
Bright.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:13.050
The implications of what happened were just
beginning to sink in.

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:18.350
Dr. Bright then called his longtime friend
Dr. Sophia Light, Site Director of the famous

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:19.740
Site-17.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:23.510
The phone call between Light and Bright was
panicked, as Jack described the emergency

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:26.120
to his friend and attempted to find a solution.

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:30.510
“We were working on that dumb little cat
thing that we were going to use in the anchor

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:31.510
trials, right?

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:32.580
Maybe two hours ago, I don't know.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.440
I was looking at it, and then I went to turn
the tail-”

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:38.110
Dr. Light immediately knew what Bright was
talking about.

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.850
“Clockwise, right?”

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:41.590
“…yes, clockwise.

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:44.611
When I turned it, uh… clockwise… it broke
in my hand.

00:06:44.611 --> 00:06:45.611
Just like that.

00:06:45.611 --> 00:06:46.611
Poof.”

00:06:46.611 --> 00:06:50.680
Dr. Light could sense that something had gone
majorly wrong, just from the way Bright emphasized

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.900
the word ‘poof’.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.700
For a few moments, Bright danced around the
implication that he was responsible for breaking

00:06:55.700 --> 00:07:00.200
the cat, hoping instead to use a less incriminating
euphemism.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.330
Light finally got him to spit it out.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.300
“They're all me!

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.370
Every single one of them, Sophia!

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:09.860
I know I'm me, obviously- I'm wearing the
amulet, but-”

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.690
Dr. Bright was cut off.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:16.010
Seconds later, he returned to the phone, clearly
relieved that he wasn’t seen by any of the

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:17.910
Bright clones that were now patrolling Site-53.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:24.460
“They're out here storming around, throwing
stuff, writing naughty words on the whiteboards.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:28.480
They're mad, every single one of them.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:31.760
The site is in lockdown, I'm sitting here
in the bathroom trying to stay out of sight,

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:34.440
and I need an evac, Sophia.”

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:39.169
Dr. Light was unamused, and asked why these
wacky events always seemed to happen while

00:07:39.169 --> 00:07:40.540
she was busy.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:45.970
Bright begged and pleaded, asking her to send
a Task Force, or to check and see what Dr.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:47.169
Mann could do.

00:07:47.169 --> 00:07:51.960
Light shot down Bright’s request, saying
that Mann was at a conference off-site.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:56.311
When Bright asked where, Light informed him
that it was at Site-53, and that he had just

00:07:56.311 --> 00:07:58.430
gotten there a few minutes ago.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:03.220
Bright paused, shuddered, and struggled to
stay calm as he informed Light that he was

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:05.240
at Site-53 too.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:10.389
This was the Site where the SCP-4498 anomaly
had taken effect!

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:13.100
The security cameras showed utter chaos across
Site-53.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:18.660
The team Dr. Mann brought alongside him to
the conference was composed of the Foundation’s

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:19.760
all-stars.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:26.060
Famous names like Dr. Gears, Agent Troy Lament,
Dr. Kain Pathos Crow, and even the infamous

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.530
Dr. Clef.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:32.760
These Foundation superstars were on the run,
being pursued by a mob of angry Jack Bright

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:40.020
SCP-4498 instances, who wielded broken furniture,
tires, and kitchen utensils in their pursuit

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.880
of the conference-goers.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:46.741
Site-53 was put on lockdown, and after several
hours of radio silence, Mobile Task Force

00:08:46.741 --> 00:08:52.440
Rhea-7 "Gate Guns" arrived to infiltrate the
Site and deescalate the situation.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:57.930
When the Task Force operatives arrived, they
immediately began to search for Dr. Bright.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:01.920
Unsurprisingly, when they called out for him,
several voices responded.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:06.180
When the Task Force lead introduced himself
and informed the instances that they were

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:12.920
sent to extract Dr. Bright, an SCP-4498 instance
that took over the body of Site-53 personnel

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:17.830
Dr. Herman Donaldson brandished a rifle, and
informed the operatives that they were all

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:18.870
Jack Bright.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:23.600
He told the Task Force to leave, and that
the situation was under control.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:28.800
As he was saying this, an explosion was heard
behind him, which the instance seemed completely

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.430
unfazed by.

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:35.160
When the Lead reiterated that they were just
there to extract Dr. Mann, his team, and the

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:40.290
real Jack Bright, the instances got upset
at the implication that they were anything

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.240
less than the genuine article.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:50.670
It was certain, SCP-4498 had taken over Site-53,
and they were the ones calling the shots.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:56.830
The Foundation’s quiet and kind Dr. Kiryu
then stood up, now affected by SCP-4498 and

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:58.980
wearing a flashy jacket and hat.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:04.100
She introduced herself as the “Pirate Queen
Jack Bright” and spoke in a heavy pirate

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:05.100
accent.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:09.550
When the Task Force attempted to breach the
site further, Dr. Kiryu and her devoted crewmates

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:14.089
fired upon them, though since they were all
Jack Brights, they were actually horrible

00:10:14.089 --> 00:10:15.089
shots.

00:10:15.089 --> 00:10:19.300
In fact, the Task Force never really felt
like they were in danger, despite being fired

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:22.700
on by several dozen SCP-4498 instances.

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:26.040
Instead, they hid themselves and waited for
backup.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:30.530
But the personnel weren’t the only ones
affected by SCP-4498.

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:35.500
Site-53 was also host to a number of sentient
humanoid anomalies, who were now harboring

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.340
the consciousness of Jack Bright.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:43.190
In fact, in an incredible stroke of bad luck,
Site-53 happened to be containing one of the

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:47.460
most famous murder monsters the Foundation
has ever faced.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:55.279
That’s right, SCP-096, the Shy Guy, had
been relocated from its original containment

00:10:55.279 --> 00:11:00.620
to Site-53, and now it possessed the mind
of Dr. Bright.

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:07.210
Security footage showed an SCP-4498 instance
being lured to SCP-096’s containment chamber.

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:13.020
SCP-096, now possessing the voice of Bright,
pretended to be a Bright instance locked inside

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:16.960
the containment chamber and asked the onlooking
instance to free it.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:21.280
The instance suspected it was a trap, but
the Bright on the other side assured him that

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:24.770
he was doing important…

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:30.370
science things and that this was certainly,
absolutely not a trap.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:37.010
Convinced by SCP-096’s amazing acting, the
SCP-4498 instance opened the chamber door

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:43.750
and let loose the SCP-4498-SCP-096 hybrid,
which threw the other Bright instance down

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:46.320
the length of the entire hallway.

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:52.089
SCP-096 was elated to run around the Site
and wreak havoc, just as the others were doing.

00:11:52.089 --> 00:11:57.200
Another Bright emerged from Site-53’s trash
receptacles, covered in waste and sewage.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:01.980
He spoke to a group of rats, encouraging them
to join him in the sewers below.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:06.390
The rat-Brights praised their new leader and
followed him into the dumpster.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:11.290
Back up front, the Brights led by Pirate Queen
Kiryu had constructed a wooden pirate ship

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:14.180
over a Foundation issue M1-Abrams tank.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:17.350
Bound and tied to the mast was Agent Troy
Lament.

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:22.970
Meanwhile, as the Brights ran rampant throughout
Site-53, Dr. Mann and his conference team

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:28.010
were couped up in a storage closet, hiding
from the chaotic mob actively looking for

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:29.010
them.

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:31.800
Needless to say, they weren’t very happy.

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:36.750
After a role call check, Dr. Mann smelled
something foul, and informed the scientist-turned

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:41.130
Golden Retriever Kain Pathos Crow to remove
his dog-butt from his face.

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:45.899
Dr. Crow then informed Mann that he was across
the closet, and that the behind belonged to

00:12:45.899 --> 00:12:46.899
someone else.

00:12:46.899 --> 00:12:52.760
In that moment, the real Dr. Jack Bright,
stinking butt and all, introduced himself,

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:56.220
causing all of the closet-crew to jump back
in shock.

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:59.980
Bright tried to reason with Mann’s crew
and begged them to let him hide.

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:03.570
But the crew started debating whether or not
they should just throw Bright to the Pirate

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:06.839
Crew for causing all of this ridiculous trouble
in the first place.

00:13:06.839 --> 00:13:12.410
Then Dr. Crow,in his infinite doggy wisdom,
came up with a solution.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:18.459
They could find the cat statue, repair it,
and get Dr. Bright to utilize SCP-963 on the

00:13:18.459 --> 00:13:24.270
cat statue, effectively freeing the Site-53
inhabitants from Bright’s consciousness.

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:29.550
Bright liked the idea, well, until he realized
that it might break the amulet in the process.

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:31.560
And with that, the crew set off.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:35.090
Meanwhile, the pirate crew was posting flyers
around the site that read:

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:37.149
“TO THE COWARD JACK BRIGHT

00:13:37.149 --> 00:13:43.839
BY THE AUTHORITY OF HER SALTIEST MAJESTY JACK
BRIGHT, Pirate Queen, Raider of the High Seas,

00:13:43.839 --> 00:13:46.420
Mad Butterfly of the Rolling Waves,

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:52.820
WE DO COMMAND YOU TO APPEAR BEFORE THE PIRATE
COUNCIL TO NEGOTIATE THE RELEASE OR BUTT-STABBING

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:55.220
AND THEN EXECUTION OF ONE:

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:56.560
TROY LAMENT

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.440
HIS CRIMES ARE NUMEROUS:

00:13:58.440 --> 00:13:59.440
Lollygagging

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:00.990
Saying Hurtful Things

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:03.440
Criticizing Queen Bright's Very Good Hat

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:06.050
THIS WON'T BE FORGIVEN

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:08.810
APPEAR OR BE BUTT STABBED”

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:12.010
Dr. Mann’s crew had no choice.

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:17.090
They appeared before the group of Bright instances
that called themselves the high council, and

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:19.550
began to negotiate for control of Site-53.

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:26.930
Dr. Mann, Gears, Bright, and Crow spoke with
Pirate Queen Kiryu and a few other Bright

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:31.720
instances, who all introduced themselves in
equally ridiculous ways.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:36.960
One was representing the Culinary Jacks of
the Kitchens and Breakrooms, whose feasts

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:40.370
were legendary and apparently very tasty!

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:44.870
Another was representing the Sneaky Darkness
Jacks of the Parts Of The Site Where The Power

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:46.320
Had Gone Out!

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:51.360
They are sneaky and very mysterious, as the
representative pointed out.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:57.820
Another was MASTER JACK, Lord of the AquaJacks,
Protector of the Toilets and Sinks!

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:02.370
Then you had the master of the rats, Filth
Jack, who asked the council to behold his

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:05.130
many armies of trash and refuse.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:09.730
And with that, the almighty council of Jack
Brights had established themselves.

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:14.670
The two groups began negotiations to rescue
Agent Troy Lament, who, as Kiryu pointed out

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:18.700
earlier, was about to be subjected to a fierce
butt-stabbing.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:26.470
As Agent Lament was brought up into the court,
Pirate Queen Bright laid out her terms: SCP-963-1,

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:29.480
the amulet that contained Bright's consciousness.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:34.170
Bright was confused, and asked why, to which
Kiryu replied that it was because they weren’t

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:38.860
sure just how long the SCP-4498 Brights were
going to last.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:43.560
They didn’t want to suddenly die off, and
with the amulet they could guarantee their

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:47.110
status as bodies of Dr. Bright forever.

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:52.850
Bright refused, and tried to appeal to reason,
stating that since they were all him, he knew

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:58.399
that deep down they were all sensible people,
known for their good instincts and controlled

00:15:58.399 --> 00:15:59.410
temperaments.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:03.930
This statement earned Bright some raised eyebrows
from Mann’s crew, who knew of the doctor’s

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:06.149
ridiculous exploits all too well.

00:16:06.149 --> 00:16:08.730
Kiryu once again asked for the amulet.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:12.850
Bright agreed, but only if they gave them
the cat statue.

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:17.180
The council of Brights reluctantly agreed,
and the exchange was made.

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:21.960
The statue was tossed to Mann’s crew, who
in response, pushed Dr. Bright into the crowd

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:27.030
of SCP-4498 instances, who promptly restrained
the Doctor.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:32.570
While Gears and the crew attempted to fix
the cat statue, Dr. Kiryu-Pirate-Queen-Bright

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:35.450
had other plans for the captured Dr. Bright.

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:39.670
Brandishing a comically large knife, she told
Bright that he was about to lose something

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:43.519
VERY important to his dignity and manhood.

00:16:43.519 --> 00:16:46.470
Bright panicked, and started to plead with
Kiryu.

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:52.000
Just in time, Gears tossed the cat statue
to Bright, who turned the tail back clockwise.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:58.020
The SCP-4498 instances jumped back, fell forward
again, and rubbed their heads.

00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:00.860
And for a brief moment, they were back to
normal!

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:04.069
Dr. Kiryu questioned her flashy pirate outfit.

00:17:04.069 --> 00:17:08.850
But because things can never work out for
Jack Bright, it was only Dr. Kiryu and Clef

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:11.610
who regained their original senses.

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:17.839
The rest of the SCP-4498 instances were too
far out of range for the cat statue to work.

00:17:17.839 --> 00:17:21.760
And then to make matters worse, the statue
disintegrated seconds later.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:27.629
Now with a restored Clef and Kiryu and a rescued
Agent Lament, Dr. Bright and the rest of Mann’s

00:17:27.629 --> 00:17:35.649
team ran out of Site-53, being chased by a
horde of angry SCP-4498 instances once more.

00:17:35.649 --> 00:17:41.000
Following their escape, Site-53 was recontained
and the current containment procedures were

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:42.000
established.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:46.470
Dr. Bright and the personnel who escaped that
day were subjected to a series of interviews.

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:52.259
Dr. Mann, being the renowned greatest surgeon
in the Foundation, gave a bombastic account

00:17:52.259 --> 00:17:56.509
of the day’s events where he downplayed
the importance and the help the members of

00:17:56.509 --> 00:17:59.580
his conference team gave him during their
escape.

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:04.509
Another member of the conference team, Dr.
Desei, was particularly upset at the apparent

00:18:04.509 --> 00:18:09.950
inefficiency of the Mobile Task Force squad
sent to reclaim Site-53, wondering why one

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:14.169
of the hundreds of more competent Task Forces
couldn’t have been sent instead to save

00:18:14.169 --> 00:18:19.220
them all from the horror of having to listen
to Jack Bright talk to himself for over 12

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:20.220
hours.

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:25.169
Dr. Sophia Light informed Dr. Bright, after
an awkward reunion between the two, that he

00:18:25.169 --> 00:18:29.299
was going back on Special Probation as a punishment
for his actions.

00:18:29.299 --> 00:18:35.490
A task involving something with a wombat,
the exact details of which are vague and nebulous.

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:39.340
Whatever the case, Dr. Bright was certainly
displeased by this.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:43.590
Agent Lament was still recovering from his
capture by the pirate Brights, and from his

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:48.279
shell shocked state, it seemed like it was
going to take him awhile to get over it.

00:18:48.279 --> 00:18:53.820
Dr. Clef, during his interview, admitted that
he was late to the site, and was only pretending

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:57.429
to be a Bright instance because he thought
it’d be entertaining.

00:18:57.429 --> 00:19:01.149
After laughing to himself about beating the
captured Troy’s body with a trout, Clef

00:19:01.149 --> 00:19:06.399
concluded his interview with a single statement:
“I love the SCP Foundation.”

00:19:06.399 --> 00:19:10.409
Now go watch “SCP Immortal Dr. Bright Explained”
and “DR.

00:19:10.409 --> 00:19:17.549
BRIGHT FOR PRESIDENT SCP-4444 - Bush v. Gore”
for more on the anomalously quirky Dr. Jack

00:19:17.549 --> 00:19:18.049
Bright!

